 "appendix": {
  "title": "Terms and decision rules at a glance",
  "body": "### API parts\n- `system` / `messages` (`user`, `assistant`) / `tools` (`name`, `description`, `input_schema`) / `tool_choice` (auto, any, specific, none)\n- `stop_reason`: `end_turn` (finished), `tool_use` (run a tool), `max_tokens` (cut off), `refusal` (refused, HTTP 200), `model_context_window_exceeded` (limit hit during generation), `pause_turn` (server-side tool to be continued)\n- `tool_result`: matched by `tool_use_id`. A failure is `is_error: true`\n- `usage`: input / output / cache_creation / cache_read tokens\n- `cache_control`: on the unchanging preamble. Hits only when the content is the same from the start\n- Batches: 50% off, within 24 hours, matched by `custom_id`\n\n### Errors\n- Retryable: 429, 529, 500, 502, 503, 504 → capped exponential backoff (jitter), follow `retry-after` / terminal: 400, 401, 403, 404 → fix it (no retry) / `refusal` is a 200 → no retry; raise and log\n\n### Choosing\n- Workflow (fixed steps) ⇄ agent (steps change). Start from the simple shape\n- Haiku (fast, cheap) / Sonnet (default) / Opus (hard). Split by step\n- Tool (operation) / skill (procedure, knowledge) / MCP (shared across clients)\n- Asking in a prompt (probabilistic) ⇄ hooks and code (deterministic). To stop something, use code\n\n### Always on the right side\n- Keys in environment variables. Never in the client\n- External data is separated from instructions. Tool permissions are minimal\n- Output is validated before use. If broken, regenerate with the error\n- Production pins the model version. Switch after evaluating\n\n### 🎓 Decision rules at a glance\n- **Streaming**: tool input is incomplete until `content_block_stop` → do not parse. Append to history after `message_stop`. If cut off, discard and retry\n- **Thinking blocks**: return unchanged in the next turn. The API rejects edits, summaries and deletions\n- **Tool results**: a failure is `is_error: true`. An empty result breeds a confident wrong answer\n- **Batch**: match by `custom_id` (order not kept). A loop over the sync API is not batch. Do not use it when someone is waiting\n- **Cache**: identical prefix, within the lifetime (5 minutes / 1 hour), minimum length (1,024). Order is tools → system → messages. Up to four breakpoints\n- **Model**: start on Sonnet and move up or down by eval. A default plus overrides on cheap signals. Pin the full ID in production\n- **Permission modes**: default / acceptEdits / plan / auto (classifier) / dontAsk (everything else auto-denied) / bypassPermissions (isolated environments only). deny > ask > allow\n- **Settings**: user `~/.claude/settings.json` / project `.claude/settings.json` / local `.claude/settings.local.json` / enterprise `managed-settings.json` (cannot be overridden)\n- **MCP**: stdio (local) / HTTP (shared, recommended) / SSE (legacy). Scopes local / user / project (`.mcp.json`) / enterprise. Permissions as `mcp__server__tool`\n- **Hooks**: PreToolUse blocks with exit code 2. PostToolUse cannot block (suited to audit logs). CLAUDE.md is “mostly,” hooks are “always”\n- **Where an extension goes**: global constraints → CLAUDE.md / path-limited → `paths` in `.claude/rules/` / must not be diluted → hooks / only when needed → Skill / exploration and parallelism → subagents (Explore and Plan do not read CLAUDE.md)\n- **Distribution**: `$CLAUDE_PROJECT_DIR`, `${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}`. The author's local deny rules and hooks are not in the package\n- **Managed Agents**: sessions stored server-side → outside ZDR and HIPAA BAA (at the time of writing). On the Agent SDK, set `settingSources` explicitly\n- **Symptom → missing technique**: wrong shape → output constraints / content off → system / unrequested structure → few-shot / breaks on edge cases → a constraint or example for that variant\n- **Context**: pruning, compaction, clearing, subagents. If degradation follows turn count, look at context before the schema\n- **Eval**: exact match (labels) / code checks (format) / LLM judge (quality; needs calibrating). One change at a time; look case by case\n- **Retries**: first ask “would waiting and resending work?” Do not double up with the SDK's automatic retries\n- **Regulated data**: HIPAA → a BAA-eligible configuration / residency → pin the region on Bedrock or Vertex / the three early questions (where processed, how logged, can settings be locked)"
 }
